CI tooling sources and licenses

Docker Engine and CLI 29.9.0 use Apache-2.0.
The CLI source is https://github.com/docker/cli/tree/v29.9.0.
The engine source is https://github.com/moby/moby/tree/v29.9.0.
Docker Buildx and Compose retain their Apache-2.0 upstream distribution licenses.
The image exporter uses the pinned Apache-2.0 Moby BuildKit distribution.
The pinned Docker distribution already supplies the release transport test tool.

Hadolint 2.14.0 uses GPL-3.0.
Its corresponding source is https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/tree/v2.14.0.
The complete upstream license is included in hadolint-LICENSE.

Helm 4.2.2 and 3.16.2 use Apache-2.0.
Their sources are https://github.com/helm/helm/tree/v4.2.2
and https://github.com/helm/helm/tree/v3.16.2.

The base image retains Go, Playwright, Node, and locked npm dependency notices.
Node.js 24.22.1 uses MIT and the bundled open-source dependency licenses.
Its complete notices remain in /usr/local/LICENSE and the npm distribution.
The source is https://github.com/nodejs/node/tree/v24.22.1.
Ubuntu packages retain their copyright and license files in /usr/share/doc.
The CI helper does not add or upgrade Go or npm project dependencies.
SonarScanner remains a separate pinned upstream CI image with its upstream notices.
